# ${{APP_NAME}}

A Go module created with Code on the Go.

## Run

Tap **Run app** in the editor toolbar, or from the terminal:

```bash
go run .
```

## Test

Tap **Run tests**, or:

```bash
go test ./...
```

## Project structure

```
${{APP_NAME}}/
  go.mod          # module ${{MODULE_PATH}}
  main.go         # entry point
  main_test.go    # table-driven test for greet
  README.md
```

This project imports only the standard library, so it builds and runs with no
network connection. Once you add a third-party import, tap **Tidy modules** to
fetch it - that step does need to be online.
